# A106 (TeraDesk via #Z, sd-tera.img, 640x480). The A48 sequence, run TWICE
# with the AES restart in between:
#
#   round 1  hover Options (260,8) -> click "Video options..." (300,170) ->
#            VOPTIONS dialog -> ST-Low radio (247,185) -> OK (347,361) ->
#            ARESCH alert -> its " OK " (280,276) -> voptions() returns 1 ->
#            chrez -> get_set_video(2): shel_write(SHW_RESCHNG, ST_LOWRES+2,
#            0) (video.c:363-365,378-379) -> wait_to_quit 2000 ms + wait(500)
#            -> appl_exit -> TeraDesk Pterm's.
#   restart  sh_main returns ShExit::RezChange instead of launching the next
#            program; the kernel's session loop runs aes::reinit() + desk::
#            reset() and re-enters sh_main, whose process_inf2 finds the same
#            `#Z` line -> TeraDesk starts again (EmuTOS gemstart.S:86-124).
#   round 2  the identical sequence a second time, to show the restart is
#            repeatable and the second session behaves like the first.
#
# Coordinates: A48's, unchanged (measurement-2026-09-21-a48/method/
# tera-a48.actions; from desktop.rsc via rscdump.py + two probe runs).
# Ticks are hz_200: 200 = 1 s. The injector only advances while an EL0
# program is the running process, so the steps scheduled during the restart
# gap fire as soon as the new TeraDesk is up.
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1400 move 260 8
2200 move 300 170
2500 down
2503 up
3100 mark C_VIDEO_DIALOG
3400 move 247 185
3700 down
3703 up
4100 mark D_STLOW_PICKED
4400 move 347 361
4700 down
4703 up
5300 mark E_ALERT
5600 move 280 276
5900 down
5903 up
6000 mark F_CONFIRMED
6100 parkbr
# --- the AES restart happens here; TeraDesk comes back on the new session ---
8200 parkbr
9000 mark I_RESTARTED
9300 move 260 8
10100 move 300 170
10400 down
10403 up
11000 mark J_VIDEO_DIALOG_2
11300 move 247 185
11600 down
11603 up
12000 move 347 361
12300 down
12303 up
12900 mark K_ALERT_2
13200 move 280 276
13500 down
13503 up
13600 mark L_CONFIRMED_2
13700 parkbr
# --- the second AES restart ---
15800 parkbr
16600 mark M_RESTARTED_2
